messages.text:
Add inputs and outputs to jobs. A job declares what it takes; small run passes it; the script reads it; whatever it writes to an output directory is captured on the run.

Schema in small.toml:

toml
[inputs]
image     = { type = "file",   required = true, accept = ".jpg,.png", help = "Photo to analyse" }
threshold = { type = "number", default = 0.5, min = 0, max = 1 }
account   = { type = "select", options = ["acme", "globex"] }
since     = { type = "date",   default = "-7d" }
label     = { type = "text",   pattern = "^[a-z0-9-]*$" }
dry_run   = { type = "bool",   default = false }

[outputs]
report = { path = "report.pdf", label = "Weekly report" }

Exactly six types. Reject anything else at small init and small deploy with a one-line error.

CLI. small run <app> --image ./photo.jpg --threshold 0.7 --dry-run. One flag per input, validated against the schema before anything is uploaded: required present, number in range, select in options, file extension in accept, text matches pattern. Files upload to the control plane; scalars go in the request body. Print the validated inputs before starting. After the run finishes, list output files with sizes and small run … --download ./out to fetch them.

Runtime. runner.py receives inputs and writes: scalars as SMALL_INPUT_<NAME> env vars (uppercase), files to $SMALL_INPUTS/<name><ext>, and everything to $SMALL_INPUTS/inputs.json. Creates $SMALL_OUTPUTS/. On exit, uploads every file in it to the control plane, declared or not.

Control plane. Store inputs on the run row as JSON; store uploaded files in R2 keyed by run id; add GET /api/runs/<id>/outputs and GET /api/runs/<id>/outputs/<name>. Cap uploads at 100 MB per run for now.

Example. Update examples/yolo-gradio into examples/yolo-job: takes image and threshold, writes annotated.jpg and boxes.json to $SMALL_OUTPUTS. Keep the Gradio one too.

Skill. Update SKILL.md: every non-secret os.environ read in a job is an input — declare it. Anything the script saves for the user goes in $SMALL_OUTPUTS.

Test. small run yolo-job --image tests/fixtures/people.jpg --threshold 0.4, assert the run row records both inputs, two output files exist, and boxes.json parses with at least one box. Assert --threshold 2 fails before upload with a range error.

Touch only runner.py, the run command, the run routes, the schema validator, the example, SKILL.md, and tests. Skip: the web form, multiple selects, outputs over 100 MB, input presets. ponytail: each. this is done?

